# examples/games/05_endless_runner, played: a run that ends at the first rock,
# then one that jumps two and ends at the third, nearly twice as far.
#
# The runner runs on its own, from 320 px/s and faster; Space (ui_accept)
# jumps. A rock is placed every 520 units run, give or take rmp::random's 120,
# so the second run's rocks, drawn after the first run's, stand where they
# stand on every run of this script and nowhere else. One rock ends a run. The
# score is the distance, ten units to the metre. See tests/e2e/script.h for the
# grammar.

# --- the failure path: no jump --------------------------------------------------

# The first rock, at 100 m.
182 expect scene RunnerScene
183 expect scene OverScene
186 shot ouch_at_the_first_rock

# Play again, with the mouse: down on 195, up on 196, the new run from 197.
195 click 400 245
195 expect scene OverScene
196 expect scene RunnerScene

# --- the happy path: two rocks jumped ---------------------------------------------

# Up when the first rock is 100 px ahead, and over it at the top of the jump.
368 tap KEY_SPACE
384 shot over_the_first_rock
# The second.
454 tap KEY_SPACE
# And no jump at the third, at 194 m.
541 expect scene RunnerScene
542 expect scene OverScene
545 shot ouch_at_the_third_rock

# Play again, from the keyboard: the button has the focus.
552 tap KEY_ENTER
552 expect scene RunnerScene
554 shot again
554 end
